      "transcriptHtml": "\n            <div class=\"font-bold text-skybrand-800 flex items-center gap-1\">📜 Transcript Task 2:</div>\n            <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Were you sporty as a child?</p>\n            <p><strong>Ironman:</strong> No, I always felt sick and weak. I had allergies, too. So I always had a runny nose and itchy skin.</p>\n            <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> When did that change?</p>\n            <p><strong>Ironman:</strong> My friends started doing sports. I wanted to, too. My sports instructor said, \"Do more exercise, or continue to feel sick. It's up to you.\"</p>\n            <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> Was it easy?</p>\n            <p><strong>Ironman:</strong> No, it was hard. I did more exercise, so my body ached. But slowly, I felt better.</p>\n            <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> What do you do now?</p>\n            <p><strong>Ironman:</strong> I do triathlons around the world. It's a tough competition. You have to swim, run, and ride a bike. I use around 6,500 calories in one event!</p>\n            <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> How do you prepare?</p>\n            <p><strong>Ironman:</strong> Three great things to do before the race are: eat more healthy food, sleep more, and do more exercise. Then you'll be ready.</p>\n          ",
